<i>Let's all sing together, gegege no ge</i>

00:01:54.440 --> 00:01:58.280
<i>minnade utaou gegege no ge</i>

00:01:58.780 --> 00:02:03.240
<i>Let's all sing together, gegege no ge</i>

00:01:58.780 --> 00:02:03.240
<i>minnade utaou gegege no ge</i>

00:02:29.190 --> 00:02:30.240
CHAPTER 41

00:02:30.730 --> 00:02:35.170
ENIGMA! THE BAKE-ZORI REBELLION

00:02:37.280 --> 00:02:38.130
Oh?

00:02:38.130 --> 00:02:40.810
Oh no! It's leaking?

00:02:40.810 --> 00:02:44.770
When you look at it,
this bowl has a lot of cracks.

00:02:44.770 --> 00:02:46.180
Hup.

00:02:46.180 --> 00:02:49.070
Maybe we should get a new one.

00:02:49.070 --> 00:02:52.650
Now, now, Kitaro.
Treat things with respect.

00:02:53.090 --> 00:02:56.600
This bowl can still be used if we fix it.

00:02:58.420 --> 00:03:01.500
In that case I'll have the cracks sealed.

00:03:01.500 --> 00:03:05.110
Ah, that would be helpful.

00:03:06.930 --> 00:03:08.910
TSUJIMURA SHOE STORE

00:03:08.910 --> 00:03:12.290
CLOSING NOTICE
THANK YOU FOR YOUR SUPPORT

00:03:12.290 --> 00:03:13.880
Oof.

00:03:13.880 --> 00:03:16.390
When are the movers coming again?

00:03:16.390 --> 00:03:18.680
They said around 4 o'clock.

00:03:18.680 --> 00:03:20.800
That doesn't give us much time.

00:03:21.110 --> 00:03:24.300
Dad! The movers will be here at 4.

00:03:24.300 --> 00:03:26.400
Hurry and sort everything.

00:03:26.400 --> 00:03:28.310
Yes, I know.

00:03:32.670 --> 00:03:36.050
I've been here a long time.

00:03:36.960 --> 00:03:39.310
How can I hurry?

00:03:42.550 --> 00:03:44.410
THINGS TO TAKE

00:04:35.190 --> 00:04:37.260
Dad, you finished?

00:04:37.260 --> 00:04:38.410
Yes.

00:04:45.280 --> 00:04:46.880
LEAVE MOVING TO US!

00:04:48.160 --> 00:04:49.940
We got a lot done today.

00:04:49.940 --> 00:04:53.140
We should start thinking about unpacking.

00:05:00.130 --> 00:05:01.530
TRASH BAG

00:05:12.810 --> 00:05:14.590
Man, what a great meal!

00:05:14.590 --> 00:05:16.670
Isao!

00:05:16.670 --> 00:05:18.540
Isao!!

00:05:18.540 --> 00:05:22.670
Isao! Where did you go, Isao?!

00:05:24.610 --> 00:05:26.060
He's not outside.

00:05:26.060 --> 00:05:28.230
Then where did they go?

00:05:28.230 --> 00:05:31.300
Were we thrown away?

00:05:31.620 --> 00:05:32.930
Impossible...

00:05:32.930 --> 00:05:35.430
How could Isao throw us away?

00:05:39.250 --> 00:05:43.970
Isao was always a kind person
who took care of his things.

00:05:44.510 --> 00:05:47.950
I was a zori sandal his dad used.

00:05:47.950 --> 00:05:51.450
He took care of me since he was a child.

00:05:54.520 --> 00:05:58.380
He opened a shoe store in Tokyo
and started a family.

00:05:58.380 --> 00:06:04.760
Even so, he said I was a good luck charm
for this store and took care of me.

00:06:05.990 --> 00:06:08.520
And yet... Why...?

00:06:08.520 --> 00:06:10.880
Because that's what humans do.

00:06:11.450 --> 00:06:12.420
Who's there?!

00:06:12.780 --> 00:06:14.270
I'm Rat Man.

00:06:14.270 --> 00:06:18.060
Listen, guys.
Don't expect too much from humans.

00:06:18.330 --> 00:06:20.760
What do you know about Isao?!

00:06:21.540 --> 00:06:23.970
I don't know about this "Isao-san."

00:06:24.840 --> 00:06:27.480
But I know all about humans.

00:06:27.630 --> 00:06:30.850
NEW MODEL SMARTPHONE BUYERS

00:06:28.090 --> 00:06:30.850
They're balls of greed
that want everything.

00:06:31.640 --> 00:06:33.500
But they quickly get bored,

00:06:33.500 --> 00:06:35.400
and throw things away.

00:06:37.730 --> 00:06:38.790
But...

00:06:39.190 --> 00:06:42.670
You may have cared enough to come alive,

00:06:42.670 --> 00:06:46.790
but if you ask me, that's what humans are.

00:06:47.360 --> 00:06:48.670
-What?!
-How dare you!

00:06:48.670 --> 00:06:50.260
Settle down now.

00:06:50.820 --> 00:06:53.850
As a fellow <i>yokai</i>,
I feel your pain all too well.

00:06:53.850 --> 00:06:56.320
So, how about this?

00:06:56.320 --> 00:06:59.770
Wanna work with me
to get back at the humans?

00:07:00.330 --> 00:07:02.550
Together, we'll be unstoppable!

00:07:03.750 --> 00:07:06.030
You can count me in!

00:07:06.030 --> 00:07:07.740
-M-Me too!
-And me!

00:07:07.740 --> 00:07:10.170
-Let's do it!
-If Isao...

00:07:10.170 --> 00:07:15.780
No, if humans are really that selfish,
I want to see it for myself.

00:07:15.780 --> 00:07:19.530
Okay! Let's get to work right away!

00:07:23.330 --> 00:07:27.700
First, I put these guys up for sale
on a classifieds site.

00:07:24.710 --> 00:07:26.710
SELLER: BIBIBI-SAN
CATEGORY: MENS, SHOES, OTHER

00:07:26.710 --> 00:07:29.720
ACTUAL ZORI USED IN
"RYOMA! THE CLOTH OF SAKAMOTO RYOMA"!

00:07:30.070 --> 00:07:35.940
What?! The actual zori that Keisuke
Takenouchi-kun wore in his movie?!

00:07:35.940 --> 00:07:37.770
Yes! I'll buy it!

00:07:36.620 --> 00:07:37.770
BUY

00:07:39.200 --> 00:07:41.930
It's Takenouchi-kun's zori!

00:07:42.420 --> 00:07:43.520
It smells so good!

00:07:44.080 --> 00:07:47.890
Now you're part of
my permanent collection.

00:07:48.420 --> 00:07:51.780
Let the dumb humans dream a little.

00:07:54.850 --> 00:07:56.120
Huh?! My zori!

00:07:56.120 --> 00:07:59.040
My zori's gone?!

00:08:00.560 --> 00:08:04.540
I won't make a lot at once,
but the income is forever.

00:08:04.560 --> 00:08:06.790
NET BANK

00:08:05.060 --> 00:08:07.160
I'll always have stock after all.

00:08:08.820 --> 00:08:10.370
Rat Man-san.

00:08:10.860 --> 00:08:12.020
What's up?

00:08:12.020 --> 00:08:15.190
This one wanted to come
so I brought it along.

00:08:15.190 --> 00:08:17.270
Sure! Let's dream the dream!

00:08:17.270 --> 00:08:19.060
Forget about the humans.

00:08:19.060 --> 00:08:21.690
They don't care about things.

00:08:21.690 --> 00:08:24.810
They won't notice if they have
three rulers and one goes missing.

00:08:26.080 --> 00:08:28.200
You guys on the other hand are admirable!

00:08:28.200 --> 00:08:32.370
You let humans use you without complaint
to help them.

00:08:32.370 --> 00:08:35.870
Your unselfishness
brings tears to my eyes.

00:08:35.870 --> 00:08:36.870
Isao...

00:08:36.870 --> 00:08:40.530
Are we really as unselfish as he says?

00:08:41.640 --> 00:08:47.910
We have a greed that makes simply
being taken care of by humans not enough.

00:08:49.070 --> 00:08:51.700
You've had too much. Are you okay?

00:08:53.260 --> 00:08:57.460
I wanted to be used as a cup forever.

00:08:59.030 --> 00:09:00.590
But, Isao...

00:09:01.330 --> 00:09:04.260
He threw us away because we were old!

00:09:05.870 --> 00:09:06.930
Yeah.

00:09:08.130 --> 00:09:09.910
Isao... No...

00:09:09.910 --> 00:09:12.600
Humans aren't worth believing in.

00:09:14.220 --> 00:09:19.740
You guys, stay sharp
and work at each of your locations.

00:09:19.740 --> 00:09:21.130
Okay!

00:09:21.130 --> 00:09:25.840
Remember, be sure not to let the humans
see you move.

00:09:25.840 --> 00:09:27.050
Okay!

00:09:27.050 --> 00:09:31.090
There's a troublemaker
we can't let know about you.

00:09:31.090 --> 00:09:34.130
Apparently, stuff is moving on its own.

00:09:34.130 --> 00:09:37.630
They must be items that gained souls,
Tsukumogami.

00:09:34.150 --> 00:09:37.630
BIZARRE! FLASHLIGHT EXCEEDS
SPEED LIMIT ON ROAD?!

00:09:37.870 --> 00:09:43.270
Recently there's been a bunch of
similar letters sent to the Yokai Mailbox.

00:09:43.270 --> 00:09:46.530
That's strange. Let's look into it.

00:09:46.530 --> 00:09:48.260
Yes, Dad.

00:09:50.460 --> 00:09:52.900
What's going on?! Didn't I tell you?!

00:09:55.130 --> 00:09:57.900
<i>You there, flashlight! Stop!</i>

00:09:58.470 --> 00:10:00.120
<i>Flashlight?!</i>

00:10:00.120 --> 00:10:03.440
100 km to Tokyo!

00:10:05.270 --> 00:10:06.670
It must've been you.

00:10:06.670 --> 00:10:07.870
I'm talking to you!

00:10:08.980 --> 00:10:12.760
Listen. Be absolutely careful
when coming back.

00:10:12.760 --> 00:10:13.640
Well?!

00:10:13.640 --> 00:10:14.910
Yessir!

00:10:15.440 --> 00:10:17.770
Are some of you guys missing?

00:10:17.770 --> 00:10:19.230
Where'd the cup go?

00:10:19.230 --> 00:10:21.540
I haven't seen him recently.

00:10:33.210 --> 00:10:36.320
Rat Man, tell me where he was sent.

00:10:36.630 --> 00:10:38.810
I'll go check up on it!

00:10:42.140 --> 00:10:44.920
Hey, you okay?! I'm here to help!

00:10:44.920 --> 00:10:45.920
You!

00:10:45.920 --> 00:10:47.090
Let's go!

00:10:47.090 --> 00:10:48.380
Sorry.

00:10:48.380 --> 00:10:51.280
I've decided to stay here.

00:10:52.770 --> 00:10:56.920
The humans here don't
treat me like an ornament.

00:10:57.280 --> 00:10:59.790
They use me as a cup.

00:11:11.330 --> 00:11:15.640
I'm sorry. Being used by humans
just makes me happy.

00:11:23.220 --> 00:11:25.580
BAKE-ZORI

00:11:26.350 --> 00:11:30.080
BAKE-FURUGETA

00:11:28.100 --> 00:11:29.050
-<i>"I'll turn this into money."</i>
-<i>"This idiocy might be hiding a genius."</i>

00:11:29.050 --> 00:11:30.080
<i>"No way."</i>

00:11:34.730 --> 00:11:36.330
Good grief!

00:11:36.980 --> 00:11:40.970
Everyone's ending up
going back to the humans.

00:11:43.090 --> 00:11:45.600
<i>"I'm staying at this home.
From Flashlight."</i>

00:11:47.660 --> 00:11:51.090
<i>Being used by humans just makes me happy.</i>

00:11:59.340 --> 00:12:02.940
Maybe we shouldn't
throw the humans away just yet...

00:12:03.930 --> 00:12:07.290
Bake-Zori, don't get any funny ideas.

00:12:07.290 --> 00:12:09.250
O-Of course not!

00:12:09.250 --> 00:12:11.210
I promise I'll come back!

00:12:11.210 --> 00:12:12.910
<i>You've got mail.</i>

00:12:15.440 --> 00:12:17.590
Good. The zori's got a buyer.

00:12:17.590 --> 00:12:18.680
Hup.

00:12:18.680 --> 00:12:20.880
The final bid is...

00:12:20.880 --> 00:12:23.380
FINAL BID: 1,000,000 YEN

00:12:23.780 --> 00:12:25.750
O-One million yen?!

00:12:26.620 --> 00:12:28.390
BUYER NAME
RODRIGUEZ BEBE

00:12:26.620 --> 00:12:28.390
This name...

00:12:29.540 --> 00:12:30.690
I knew it!

00:12:30.290 --> 00:12:33.390
THE SPECTACULAR WORLD OF RODRIGUEZ BEBE

00:12:30.690 --> 00:12:33.390
The avant-garde artist, Rodriguez Bebe.

00:12:34.630 --> 00:12:38.150
Super celebrity monetary sense is nuts!

00:12:39.800 --> 00:12:41.780
I don't get it at all.

00:12:41.780 --> 00:12:44.410
ANOTHER SIDE...
"AN OCCULT FREAK WHO BELIEVES IN <i>YOKAI</i>!"

00:12:44.410 --> 00:12:47.110
"ITEMS USED FOR MY STRAW ART
IS ALL JUST JUNK!!"

00:12:54.390 --> 00:12:58.660
If he's nice,
maybe I'll stick around for a while.

00:13:17.500 --> 00:13:18.470
Ow!

00:13:33.980 --> 00:13:35.710
Wonderful.

00:13:36.190 --> 00:13:41.590
With old straw work like this,
I can complete it.

00:13:43.440 --> 00:13:47.840
My antique soul art!

00:13:54.580 --> 00:13:56.230
Are you a <i>yokai</i>?

00:13:56.230 --> 00:13:58.430
L-Let go!

00:14:14.930 --> 00:14:16.880
There's no use running.

00:14:16.880 --> 00:14:19.700
You're just an old, worn-out zori.

00:14:20.190 --> 00:14:24.960
I bet your former owner couldn't use you
and put you up for sale!

00:14:24.960 --> 00:14:27.980
You abandoned zori monster!

00:14:27.980 --> 00:14:30.840
You have no home anymore!

00:14:32.370 --> 00:14:36.470
If anyone's to blame,
it's the owner who threw you away.

00:14:49.010 --> 00:14:50.710
Wait! Calm down!

00:14:50.710 --> 00:14:52.120
Let's talk this over!

00:14:52.120 --> 00:14:54.870
What do you know about Isao?!

00:14:55.140 --> 00:14:57.750
Th-This can't be happening!

00:14:57.750 --> 00:15:02.000
Somebody tell me
how to return this zori!

00:15:04.900 --> 00:15:06.260
Why...

00:15:07.780 --> 00:15:12.290
Why did you throw us away, Isao?!

00:15:13.510 --> 00:15:16.270
Wh-What did I do?

00:15:16.270 --> 00:15:21.400
We checked and all the Tsukumogami
came from you.

00:15:21.400 --> 00:15:24.320
You're this seller,
"BiBiBi-san" aren't you?!

00:15:24.320 --> 00:15:25.940
Also, this!

00:15:25.940 --> 00:15:30.030
Isn't this your customer's house?!
Explain this!

00:15:25.960 --> 00:15:30.030
MONSTER ZORI APPEARS
IN ARTIST'S HOUSE!!

00:15:30.030 --> 00:15:31.540
Th-This is...!

00:15:31.540 --> 00:15:34.160
Let's hear the details.

00:15:34.560 --> 00:15:36.190
Spill it!

00:15:40.640 --> 00:15:41.660
Hey!

00:15:49.740 --> 00:15:53.000
Answer me! Where is Isao?!

00:15:54.490 --> 00:15:56.560
H-Help us!

00:16:00.870 --> 00:16:02.820
Where is he?!

00:16:02.820 --> 00:16:04.650
Stop, Bake-Zori!

00:16:05.840 --> 00:16:06.900
Who's there?!

00:16:06.900 --> 00:16:09.280
I'm GeGeGe no Kitaro.

00:16:09.280 --> 00:16:12.250
Bake-Zori, stop your rampage now!

00:16:12.250 --> 00:16:13.360
Shut up!

00:16:13.890 --> 00:16:15.320
Don't get in my way!

00:16:18.100 --> 00:16:19.830
Spirit Hair Chanchanko!

00:16:19.920 --> 00:16:20.900
What?!

00:16:35.490 --> 00:16:38.430
Why did you go crazy
in front of the humans?

00:16:44.790 --> 00:16:47.980
I was just heartbroken.

00:16:48.840 --> 00:16:52.480
I always thought Isao cared about me...

00:16:53.300 --> 00:16:56.870
<i>It's the zori-san Dad kept
as a good luck charm.</i>

00:16:56.870 --> 00:17:01.000
And yet, I was abandoned by Isao...

00:17:01.000 --> 00:17:02.370
Why...

00:17:06.400 --> 00:17:08.330
You've got the wrong idea!

00:17:09.150 --> 00:17:14.790
Zori-san, we came here today
to take all of you with us.

00:17:16.620 --> 00:17:17.630
What?

00:17:52.860 --> 00:17:55.870
We meet again, zori-san.

00:18:12.960 --> 00:18:17.520
Dad meant to give you to a friend of his.

00:18:18.470 --> 00:18:20.020
I didn't realize...

00:18:20.850 --> 00:18:25.360
and I put you all in the trash by mistake.

00:18:25.980 --> 00:18:28.130
I'm really sorry.

00:18:28.130 --> 00:18:31.630
It's my fault for not telling him.

00:18:33.070 --> 00:18:35.350
Please don't blame my son.

00:18:35.350 --> 00:18:39.510
Then... You didn't abandon us after all?

00:18:42.990 --> 00:18:48.510
You've been with me for so long.
I'd never throw you away so easily.

00:18:50.790 --> 00:18:52.110
Isao...

00:18:54.710 --> 00:19:00.160
I'm not much use as a zori
or a good luck charm.

00:19:00.160 --> 00:19:01.560
But I...

00:19:02.470 --> 00:19:06.370
I want to be with you forever!

00:19:16.780 --> 00:19:17.970
Zori-san...

00:19:19.280 --> 00:19:22.810
They tell me I don't have much time left.

00:19:22.810 --> 00:19:23.720
What?

00:19:23.720 --> 00:19:29.220
Compared to yours,
a human's life is so short.

00:19:29.830 --> 00:19:33.240
That's why, even after I'm gone,

00:19:33.240 --> 00:19:39.270
I wanted you to be with someone who would
need you from the bottom of their heart.

00:19:42.050 --> 00:19:47.290
I never realized
you cared this much about us, Isao...

00:19:47.290 --> 00:19:49.070
Zori-san.

00:19:49.940 --> 00:19:53.380
I'm grateful to you.

00:19:53.380 --> 00:19:57.330
Whenever I was unsure, I'd look at you...

00:19:57.730 --> 00:20:01.790
and I'd sense my dead father.
It was so reassuring.

00:20:03.570 --> 00:20:08.130
You were there with me for so long.

00:20:08.660 --> 00:20:10.470
Thank you so much.

00:20:12.170 --> 00:20:13.680
Isao...

00:20:14.170 --> 00:20:17.190
IN MOURNING

00:20:57.460 --> 00:20:59.140
Thank you.

00:21:23.110 --> 00:21:25.090
FOLKLORE MUSEUM

00:21:25.090 --> 00:21:28.220
This is a straw zori.

